// NEGATIVE TEST — `p.01` is not a way to write `p.1` (N4-12).
//
// The lexer parses the digits and hands the parser an `i64`, so the SPELLING is
// gone — but the span is not, and an index written with leading zeros covers more
// source than its value has digits. Without that check `p.01` compiled silently
// as `.1`: a typo that changes which element a program reads, with no diagnostic
// anywhere.
fn main() {
    let p = (1, 2);
    print_int(p.01);
}
